          "turn_index": 0,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Burning when I pass urine, plus a temperature and back pain since yesterday. How urgent is this, and what does guidance describe for treatment?",
          "answer": "**How urgent is this?** The urgency check rated this as routine, but that is not a clearance. The urinary tract infection guidance says that fever and back or side pain are the features that move a urinary infection out of the routine category and into a more serious kind, where the kidneys may be involved (*Urinary tract infection*, General clinical reference). Your symptoms include both, so please contact a doctor or urgent care today rather than waiting.\n\n**Seek emergency help now** if you develop any of these, which the sepsis guidance lists as signs of a life-threatening response to infection (*Sepsis: signs of a life-threatening response to infection*):\n- Confusion, unusual drowsiness, or slurred speech\n- Fast breathing or breathlessness\n- A fast heartbeat, or dizziness when you stand\n- Not passing urine for many hours\n- Shivering, feeling very cold, or a very high temperature\n- Skin that looks mottled, very pale, or blue, or a rash that does not fade when pressed\n\n**What the guidance says about treatment:** The uncomplicated urinary tract infection guidance (*Uncomplicated urinary tract infection: treatment, culture indications and recurrence*) describes treatment choices made by a clinician, usually after a urine test. It says symptoms typically improve within 48 hours, and that if they do not, you should be reassessed and have a urine culture rather than simply continuing the same course. It does not give doses, and I cannot recommend any medicine. A clinician needs to make that decision with you.\n\n**What these sources do not cover:** They do not explain what is causing your symptoms in your case, how a clinician would confirm it, or what treatment suits you. Those questions are for a clinician who can examine you and test your urine.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
